From: AshesTom <258768419+AshesTom@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] comctl32: draw SysLink's links in COLOR_HOTLIGHT

Purpose: links of the Security Center and other pages are in XP's link
colour, not in the selection's.
Windows behavior: XP's comctl32 6 draws SysLink's links in COLOR_HOTLIGHT
(a link painted with WM_PRINTCLIENT after SetSysColors gave COLOR_HIGHLIGHT
and COLOR_HOTLIGHT different values: the link is COLOR_HOTLIGHT's).
Wine before: COLOR_HIGHLIGHT, the selection colour (grey with Luna's
Silver, olive with its olive).
Change: COLOR_HOTLIGHT for links and visited links.
Scope: comctl32 6's SysLink.
---
diff --git a/dlls/comctl32_v6/syslink.c b/dlls/comctl32_v6/syslink.c
--- a/dlls/comctl32_v6/syslink.c
+++ b/dlls/comctl32_v6/syslink.c
@@ -2266,8 +2266,9 @@
         infoPtr->HasFocus = FALSE;
         infoPtr->MouseDownID = -1;
         infoPtr->TextColor = comctl32_color.clrWindowText;
-        infoPtr->LinkColor = comctl32_color.clrHighlight;
-        infoPtr->VisitedColor = comctl32_color.clrHighlight;
+        /* Windows' links are COLOR_HOTLIGHT (XP's comctl32 6, measured). */
+        infoPtr->LinkColor = comctl32_color.clrHotTrackingColor;
+        infoPtr->VisitedColor = comctl32_color.clrHotTrackingColor;
         infoPtr->BreakChar = ' ';
         infoPtr->IgnoreReturn = infoPtr->Style & LWS_IGNORERETURN;
         TRACE("SysLink Ctrl creation, hwnd=%p\n", hwnd);
